course: dictionary
lesson: 10134
title: Three: a number, a word and a sign
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Three is the number 3, one more than two. «A legend says three brothers, Kyi, Shchek and Khoryv, and their sister Lybid founded the city.» Count the names: there are three brothers, so three tells you how many.
explain: The same word can mean different things. A third is one of three equal parts, and it is also the place after second. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: In casual talk, «a three» can be a basket worth 3 points, and «three's a crowd» means two friends want to be alone. In formal writing, you may meet «thrice», which means three times.
fact: Three is the number 3, one more than two.
fact: A third is one of three equal parts, and it is also the place after second.
fact: «Three times» means 3 times, as in «three times as many», and «thrice» means the same in formal writing.
fact: A «three» can be the digit 3, a card or die face with 3 on it, or a basket worth 3 points.
fact: «Three's a crowd» is a casual saying that means two friends want to be alone.
exercise: «The Zebra and the Giraffe count "One--two--three!" and vanish.» What number do they finish counting on? | One | Two | Four | *Three
exercise: What is a third? | A triangle with 3 sides | A card with the number 2 | *One of three equal parts | A basket worth 3 points
exercise: «Imagine a sloth that can swim across a river about three times faster than it climbs.» What does «three times faster» mean? | *About 3 times as fast | Three hours slower | Exactly three seconds faster | Three times in the same river
test: Which word means «three times» in formal writing? | Threesies | *Thrice | Three's a crowd | Triangle
test: In basketball, what is «a three»? | *A basket worth 3 points | A card with the number 2 | A bad shot that misses | A team with only three players
exam: Which word in a formal text means «three times»? | Three's a crowd | Threepeat | *Thrice | Threesies
